<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime entitlements. Used only when CI signs: unsigned builds ignore this.
  The same file goes to helpers (entitlementsInherit), since the utilityProcess that
  runs the webmail server is a helper and runs Node with V8's JIT.

  allow-jit: V8 needs MAP_JIT memory in every process that runs JavaScript.
  allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8's WebAssembly tiers and the Electron helpers
    still ask for it. The local mail store is SQLite in WebAssembly, so it's needed.

  Left out on purpose, after checking what the app does:
  - keychain-access-groups. safeStorage uses the login keychain through the legacy
    SecKeychain calls, whose access follows the code signature. It needs no entitlement.
    The native helper's Touch ID path adds it with a provisioning profile if it starts
    keeping keys in the data protection keychain.
  - disable-library-validation. Every .node and .dylib in the bundle, the server's
    sharp included, is signed with the app's own team when the bundle is signed.
  - allow-dyld-environment-variables, debugger, automation, camera and microphone. The
    app has no use for any of them.
  - app-sandbox and network entitlements. Those are for the Mac App Store. This is a
    Developer ID build.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
